presentation"><path class="RatingStar__fill" d="M24 9.63469C24 9.35683 23.7747 9.13158 23.4969 9.13158H15.0892L12.477 1.34327C12.4269 1.19375 12.3095 1.0764 12.16 1.02625C11.8966 0.937894 11.6114 1.07983 11.523 1.34327L8.91088 9.13158H0.503157C0.33975 9.13158 0.186521 9.21094 0.0922364 9.3444C-0.0680877 9.57134 -0.0140806 9.88529 0.212865 10.0456L7.00408 14.8432L4.40172 22.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4595809465">January 9, 2024</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">Filthy Royal is book four in the Ruthless Warlords series by Alison Aimes. This book also contained the prequel, Filthy Beginnings which is highly recommended you read first. You really need the back story to experience the impact of what is happening in Filthy Royal. This is an alpha/omega romance. It can be read as a stand alone BUT I’ve read the whole series and it’s amazing. You would definitely enjoy this more if you have met the rest of the Skolov family and gotten to know them.<br><br><img alt="" src="https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1686267015i/34341690._SY540_.jpg" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br>Damien Skolov is the fourth and youngest brother in the Skolov family. When we first meet him in the prequel, he is eighteen years old and is a cage fighter, trying to win the grand prize for his family. But all his plans are thrown in the wind when he walks past HER! The dancer in the cage. The prize. His mate. Suddenly all that matters is her.<br><br>Scarlett is twenty one when we first meet her. She has never known life outside of the dome, outside of captivity. She has been trained and groomed to be the prize. And now it’s time. Only as soon as the alpha male crashes against the glass of her cage, she feels it. The unmistakable yearning for the alpha that is her fated mate. Only things don’t go as planned. Both Scarlett and Damien are merely pawns in a very ugly, twisted game. <br><br>Four years pass at the start of Filthy Royal. The Skolov family has finally risen the ranks in the Brotherhood. Damien is now the Skolov enforcer, and works hard to be worthy of his family. They are a close knit family. I love these siblings by the way. <br><img src="https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1505147277i/23891063.jpg" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br>Scarlett is no longer a dancer. Her situation is worse than ever and she has spent the last four years plotting and planning to take those that have hurt her and her brother, Luc down. But then her life is thrown into turmoil when a certain alpha comes literally crashing back into her life. A very angry alpha that wants revenge.<br><br><img alt="" src="https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1686267015i/34341689._SY540_.jpg" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br>One thing about Alison’s books...you need an ice bath handy when you read them. This book is scorching hot. But it was also sweet, swoony and had some of the most romantic moments. Don’t get me wrong, there are plenty of gritty battles and lots of suspense. I especially like what Alison did with Scarlett’s brother, Luc. I would especially enjoy maybe a separate novella about his future life sometime. ‘hint hint’<br><br><img src="https://images.gr-assets.com/hostedimages/1667044376ra/33552654.gif" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"><br><br>So, if you want a book that will keep you on the edge of your seat, make you fan yourself, but also make your tummy fill with butterflies, this is for you. We also get a tiny sneak peek into the next book, Enemy Princess. I can’t wait for Anya’s story!!!<br><br><b>
  <i>“In this lifetime, in the next, and in every one after that, I will always find you.”</i>
</b><br><br>For more about this book and so many others, come and visit me at Carol's Crazy Bookish World.<br><a target="_blank" rel="noopener nofollow" href="https://www.facebook.com/groups/CarolsCrazyBookishWorld">https://www.facebook.com/groups/Carol...</a><br><br><img src="https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/hostedimages/1502304251i/23548582.jpg" class="gr-hostedUserImg" loading="lazy"></span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/10717098?shelf=paranormal-fantasy" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">paranormal-fantasy</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">61 likes</span></button></div><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">8 comments</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444272,9.65642083 L19.1708204,9.70920723 C19.4523479,10.2722622 19.4523479,10.9350066 19.1708204,11.4980616 L19.118034,11.6036344 L19.1708204,11.7092072 C19.4523479,12.2722622 19.4523479,12.9350066 19.1708204,13.4980616 L19.118034,13.6036344 L19.17