16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5726126438">July 29, 2023</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">I thought, “This is book 4. Alison Aimes is not going to shock me with a foreshadowed plot twist again.” Well, aren’t I a fool because she did! MULTIPLE TIMES!<br /><br /><b>MAIN CHARACTER NAMES AND AGES</b><br />Scarlett (25) <b>|</b> Damien Skolov (22)<br /><br /><b>FEATURES</b><br />∘ sci-fi mafia romance<br />∘ omegaverse<br />∘ second chance<br />∘ fated mates<br />∘ lovers to enemies to lovers<br />∘ fmc sort of held prisoner by mmc<br />∘ dual virgins 🤭<br /><br /><b>REVIEW</b><br />Second chance romance is one of my least favorite tropes (top spot goes to cheating). In fact, if I see a romance is second chance, I will usually skip it. Sci-fi romances get a lot of leeway with me because damned if this didn’t make me reevaluate my hatred. <br /><br />I hate second chance romance when the breakup is all angst and silly miscommunication, but when she betrays him to literally save his life? Yeah, I vibed. Furthered by the fact BOTH waited for the other, even though Damien “hated” Scarlett (his perception of the situation made this fair), I guess my new motto is “I hate second chance romance ASTERISK.”<br /><br />Watching Scarlett and Damien rebuild trust and clear up the past was refreshing. Scarlett broke my heart because of the burdens she’s been forced to shoulder since he’s been gone (and her entire life to be honest). <br /><br />I did feel the story was a <i>bit</i> drawn out due to inner monologues of “I’m a monster.” It’s frustrating to read the same thoughts over and over. And over. AND OVER. Perhaps I would’ve had a lot more patience for it if I hadn’t just got done reading <a href="https://goodreads.com/book/show/59855919.Broken_Heir__Ruthless_Warlords___3_" title="Broken Heir (Ruthless Warlords, #3) by Alison Aimes" rel="noopener">Broken Heir</a>, where it did the same thing.<br /><br />Regardless of extended angst, the storyline was strong. We learn more about what the series antagonist has been up to (aside from tormenting the Skolovs), and he suffered major blows in this one. It was so satisfying watching the Skolovs win a battle.<br /><br />This series has filled a void in me left by another, and I cannot wait to see what’s going to happen next. <br /><br /><b>OW/OM DRAMA</b> <i>minor OM</i> — Damien is very jealous of Scarlett’s husband even though they are married in title only<br /><b>CHEATING</b> technically yes with each other— Scarlett and Damien start a relationship even though she is married; HOWEVER, the marriage was forced and neither love each other in that way<br /><b>THIRD ACT BREAKUP</b> none<br /><b>ENDING</b> HEA — near future epilogue<br /><br /><b>POV</b> dual / third person<br /><b>SPICE LEVEL</b> 4 / 5<br /><b>RATING</b> 4.5 / 5</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/145247010?shelf=alien" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">alien</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/145247010?shelf=betrayal" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">betrayal</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/145247010?shelf=captivity" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">captivity</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span> <div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--ta