3095 1.0764 12.16 1.02625C11.8966 0.937894 11.6114 1.07983 11.523 1.34327L8.91088 9.13158H0.503157C0.33975 9.13158 0.186521 9.21094 0.0922364 9.3444C-0.0680877 9.57134 -0.0140806 9.88529 0.212865 10.0456L7.00408 14.8432L4.40172 22.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span><span class="baseClass RatingStar--small"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" role="presentation"><path class="RatingStar__fill" d="M24 9.63469C24 9.35683 23.7747 9.13158 23.4969 9.13158H15.0892L12.477 1.34327C12.4269 1.19375 12.3095 1.0764 12.16 1.02625C11.8966 0.937894 11.6114 1.07983 11.523 1.34327L8.91088 9.13158H0.503157C0.33975 9.13158 0.186521 9.21094 0.0922364 9.3444C-0.0680877 9.57134 -0.0140806 9.88529 0.212865 10.0456L7.00408 14.8432L4.40172 22.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4465156047">October 26, 2023</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">“𝚃𝚑𝚎 𝚖𝚘𝚜𝚝 𝚍𝚊𝚗𝚐𝚎𝚛𝚘𝚞𝚜 𝚝𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚐 𝚒𝚗 𝚝𝚑𝚒𝚜 𝚐𝚊𝚕𝚊𝚡𝚢 𝚒𝚜 𝚖𝚎 𝚠𝚑𝚎𝚗 𝙸’𝚖 𝚔𝚎𝚙𝚝 𝚏𝚛𝚘𝚖 𝚢𝚘𝚞.”<br /><br /><i>Filthy Royal </i>might just be the most intense and twisty book in this series! It was a wild ride from the first page—but one with rich emotion and character growth. (Miraculously, it also managed to sidestep every major complaint I usually have about second chance romances. 🤯)<br /><br />✱::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::✱<br /><br />𝗠𝗠𝗖: Damien, 18➞22, Cage fighter and Enforcer. Fourth brother of the Skolov dynasty, with a lot to prove.<br />𝗙𝗠𝗖: Scarlett, 21➞25, Dancer, Omega prize, and secret weapon. Like all the Omega FMCs in this series, she has cool powers. <i>(This will sound random, but she's kinda like a cross between Rainbow-Brite and <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="3966c94f-cbcf-486d-81d8-5060f07a03eb" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="3966c94f-cbcf-486d-81d8-5060f07a03eb">Quake (aka Daisy Johnson).</label>)</i><br /><br />𝗡𝗼𝘁𝗲𝘀:<i><b> | </b>omegaverse<b> | </b>insta/fated mates<b> | </b>betrayal<b> | </b>second chance<b> | </b>jealous/ possessive/ protective/ tortured mmc<b> | </b>protective/ tortured fmc<b> | </b>interrogation<b> | </b>secrets+plot twists<b> | </b>rut haze<b> | </b>dirty talk+praise<b> | </b>enemies while lovers<b> | </b>danger banging<b> | </b>double virgins<b> | </b>high action<b> | </b></i><br /><br /><i><b> | </b>free on Kobo Plus<b> | </b>~149k words<b> | </b>568 Kindle pages<b> | </b>17:05 audiobook<b> | </b></i><br /><br />✱::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::✱<br /><br />The first third of <i>Filthy Royal </i> is actually a prequel. That may sound like overkill, but it really works here, for two main reasons: For one, we get to see all of their early relationship 'firsts'. With most second chances, I usually feel partially cheated out of those milestones.<i> (C'mon—what's better than New Relationship Energy?)</i><br /><br />For another, fewer flashbacks! In fairness, flashbacks can be powerful. For example, each flashback in <i>Ruthless King</i> was a clue that advanced the plot. But second chance books are notorious for shoehorning in momentum-killing flashbacks. But here, we live each stolen moment in their (temporarily) doomed whirlwind love affair. 🥹<br /><br />... NGL it's heartbreaking that they were apart four hellish years. That said, the logic behind their separation was actually solid. There really weren't any good alternatives, something that becomes even more evident once the whole story comes out. Also, it kills me to say this because I loved younger Damien, <i>but... </i>He truly was too immature, too hot-headed, to navigate the situation they were in at the time. Even if Scarlett had made different choices, it likely would've ended worse for them. <br /><br />When they meet up again, rut haze comes on hard—at the same time all hells break loose. They're in the middle of a battle, horny and totally unhinged—and Damien's poor brother Maddox has to keep them alive while trying to talk them down 💀. It was intense but also kinda hilarious. Maddox had some great comic moments in this book. <br /><br />Understandably, Damien is still tortured and furious over the events in the prequel, but it was tough to witness how cruel he sometimes seemed. (Thankfully, it was more bark than bite.) And I was a little frustrated by Scarlett's fatalism and distrust, but she also had good reasons. They had so many obstacles, both internal and external—but it made for a very hard-won HEA.<br /><br />✱::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::✱<br /><br /><b>🎙</b>𝗔𝘂𝗱𝗶𝗼 𝗡𝗼𝘁𝗲𝘀: I got the chance to listen to an advanced copy, and it's epic. Just like the previous three books, it's narrated in <b>duet </b>by Jason Clarke and Stella Hunter. IYKYK—but in case you're not familiar, they are two of the best narrators around. Duet narration always brings an extra layer of realism, and combined with such powerful acting—holy hell, I was totally hooked. <br /><br />This book in particular really plays to Jason's range. He's pitch-perfect for the flirty, playful energy of younger Damien—and the tortured, jaded Alpha he matures into. <br /><br />And really, there's nothing Jason Clarke's voice can't do. He could narrate a livestream of paint drying, and I'd be captivated. He could read the U.S. Tax Code, and I'd be riveted. He could narrate a cookbook on <i>boiling water</i>, and I'd feel the steam... <i>Okay, okay... </i>I'll quit before it gets weird. 😝<br /><br />✱::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::✱<br /><br /><b>🚦 Safety (⚠ 𝒔𝒑𝒐𝒊𝒍𝒆𝒓𝒔!):</b><br /><br />» 𝙢𝙖𝙞𝙣 𝙥𝙪𝙧𝙨𝙪𝙚𝙧: MMC<br />» 𝙤𝙬 / 𝙤𝙢 / 𝙤𝙥: Some OM. At the end of the prequel, Scarlett <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="fddfff94-0c9b-4309-965b-b7aaee85ece3" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="fddfff94-0c9b-4309-965b-b7aaee85ece3">is forced to marry—but it's a lavender marriage. so she and Kadon are just friends. Contractually speaking, there's cheating on both sides, but neither of them consider it to be. It takes a while before Damien learns the whole story, so he's wildly jealous.</label><br />» 𝙥𝙪𝙨𝙝 / 𝙥𝙪𝙡𝙡 / 𝙖𝙣𝙜𝙨𝙩: So much angst, I had to remind myself a few times that there would be an HEA! In general: For the first third (prequel), <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="aae5bfde-fdc2-4970-b07f-d5b4dd6221ab" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="aae5bfde-fdc2-4970-b07f-d5b4dd6221ab">Damien pursues hard and Scarlett is wary. In the middle third, both push away for different reasons. In the last third, Damien is all-in.</label><br />» 𝙨𝙚𝙥𝙖𝙧𝙖𝙩𝙞𝙤𝙣: Yes, a four-year separation following the prequel. After that, <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="497176ae-1051-4475-a786-c3a16a33f2ce" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="497176ae-1051-4475-a786-c3a16a33f2ce">NO separation, beyond a few hours.</label><br />» 𝟯𝙧𝙙 𝙖𝙘𝙩 𝙬𝙤𝙗𝙗𝙡𝙚: Mainly external conflict. This book has a lot of wobbles! IMO the climax is when <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="cedf22ca-6592-41d7-a28e-f072a453b391" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="cedf22ca-6592-41d7-a28e-f072a453b391">Scarlett is kidnapped and confronts her longtime tormentor (Darvish), while Damien and crew attempt rescue.</label><br />» 𝙚𝙣𝙙𝙞𝙣𝙜: HFN. <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="8f43004f-7c6d-4dd8-8c2c-a509031076f7" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="8f43004f-7c6d-4dd8-8c2c-a509031076f7">Maybe a day later? Spicy-sweet scene, then Scarlett tells him she's pregnant. The brevity and lack of any time jump was slightly disappointing. Since there's an overarching story, I only expected a HFN, but after all their struggles, I wanted to wallow in their happiness a bit longer. And I wanted them off that damn planet, safe at home on Abzal. </label> Heads up, if you read past these lines: <input type="checkbox" class="spoiler__control" aria-label="The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide." onchange="this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);" id="9ad1d876-1db7-4b3a-b9ad-b6062d38eab9" /><label aria-hidden="true" class="spoiler" for="9ad1d876-1db7-4b3a-b9ad-b6062d38eab9">[Knock.