6 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span><span class="baseClass RatingStar--small"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" role="presentation"><path class="RatingStar__fill" d="M24 9.63469C24 9.35683 23.7747 9.13158 23.4969 9.13158H15.0892L12.477 1.34327C12.4269 1.19375 12.3095 1.0764 12.16 1.02625C11.8966 0.937894 11.6114 1.07983 11.523 1.34327L8.91088 9.13158H0.503157C0.33975 9.13158 0.186521 9.21094 0.0922364 9.3444C-0.0680877 9.57134 -0.0140806 9.88529 0.212865 10.0456L7.00408 14.8432L4.40172 22.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5828623350">October 26, 2023</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">(audiobook) Knowing what their backstory was, I was curious to see how Damien and Scarlett would reconnect. It was going to be difficult. The book didn’t disappoint.<br /><br />The author continues the Skolov story: they are still looking for their younger sister who was kidnapped. That means finding their half-brother. It’s Damien’s job as the family’s enforcer, and he crosses Scarlett’s path again, four years after her betrayal. There’s no love lost between them. Or is there?<br /><br />For various reasons, they keep secrets from each other. Secrets that would help clearing the air. It was frustrating, of course, that a single conversation could have prevented a lot of what happens to them in this book, and could have minimized their resentment. A conversation that never really happens. However, there wouldn’t be as much tension, nor much of a story. Also Damien doesn’t trust Scarlett anymore, and Scarlett’s secrets involve other people that she protects. It’s understandable that they wouldn’t want that conversation.<br /><br />I enjoyed the whole side story–that becomes part of the main story–about Scarlett’s powers. In the prequel, we saw that she didn’t really understand it. In this book, she uses them but still has little control over them. They’re more like a curse for her, to be honest. But her meeting again with Damien will make her reevaluate the situation. And not really with Damien’s help, which was an interesting touch. All in all, in this series, omegas’ powers are more metaphores for women’s attributes than anything else.<br /><br />Damien, on the other hand, is still kind of searching for his place in the family. He’s reckless because he always has something to prove. Which makes one particular scene near the end of the book absolutely beautiful. Let’s just say, he already has a place in his family, despite what he thinks. He isn’t alone.<br /><br />I loved Damien. He’s young and brutal and angry. But his tough facade hides a mushy heart, one that was broken by Scarlett and that he’s kept from everyone since. He isn’t a soft man, but he loves fiercely.<br /><br />There was a lot going on in this book besides the love story. The conspiracy–which explains what happened in the prequel and since then–is the most important part, but it has ramifications. Since it involves their half-brother, the whole Skolov family is concerned. And the second love story made me crave for more. A couple of twists finished the story beautifully.<br /><br />The series’s narrators come back, and they nail it. The female narrator expresses both the strength and the vulnerabilities of Scarlett with talent, and the male narrator is perfect for any growly alpha males, even those with a big heart. An entertaining and well done audiobook.<br /><br />Quickie<br /><br />- Series: Ruthless warlords #4 (can be read as a standalone)<br />- Hashtags: #SF romance #mafia romance #second chance romance #omegaverse #aliens #fated mates #virgin<br />- Triggers: lots of violence, abuse and death, mention of past extreme child abuse, female trafficking, cheating (technically)<br />- Main couple: Scarlett &amp; Damien Skolov<br />- Hotness: 5/5<br />- Romance: 5/5<br />- + where do I start? secondary gay couple… extremely romantic alpha male… weirdly perfect family…<br />- – lack of communication as the main problem between the characters isn’t my favorite</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContainer"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium Button--subdued"><span class="Button__labelItem">4 likes</span></button></div></div><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444272,9.65642083 L19.1708204,9.70920723 C19.4523479,10.2722622 19.4523479,10.9350066 19.1708204,11.4980616 L19.118034,11.6036344 L19.1708204,11.7092072 C19.4523479,12.2722622 19.4523479,12.9350066 19.1708204,13.4980616 L19.118034,13.6036344 L19.1708204,13.7092072 C19.4523479,14.2722622 19.4523479,14.9350066 19.1708204,15.4980616 L19,15.8397024 L19,16.1036344 C19,16.7361314 18.6701344,17.3185188 18.1373501,17.6453922 L17.9472136,17.7