ss="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4792370132">June 17, 2023</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">Filthy and sweet, with high adrenaline and full of emotions. Filthy Royal was a thrilling ride that I didn't want to exit from.<br /><br />The book begins with the prequel, Filthy Beginnings, which highlights the fast paced and, somewhat unusual, courtship that transpires between Damien and Scarlett.<br /><br />Scarlett is Consortium property and is set as part of the winnings, a prize to be won, in the tournament of cage fighters entering a galactic fighting tournament. She's a beautiful dancer that shimmers colors and is kept in a glass cage. Her entire life has been under Consortium rule and her only hope is to be won by a fair and just fighter, which she knows is unlikely, or to escape. With odds stacked against her, she would still rather try to run than give up her life to a brute. That is until she meets Damien.<br /><br />Enter Damien Skolov, a young fighter with nothing to his name and proving his worth through using his fists. Damien originally only entered the tournament to win the cash prize, but the moment he sees Scarlett he's sucked into her orbit and the mating heat hits both of them hard and fast. While he still wants the money, he also wants to win Scarlett and her freedom. He's young and impetuous, but he's also gentle and sweet when it comes to Scarlett. Yes, he also shows her how dirty he can be without jeopardizing her actual purity, and let me tell you, these two burn for one another.<br /><br />Their quick time at the tournament blazes hot and fast and there is a lot that transpires due to the quickness of their time together, there is also a lot that happens that also tears them apart just as quickly. This beginning part of the story shapes their future and jump starts their destiny to how they meet again, but under very different circumstances. It's heartbreaking, but I LOVED how Alison set up this part of the story to continue on with the rest. <br /><br />I loved Damien Skolov (his brother Maddox and sister Anya too, but for now I'm just going to focus on Damien). He is an Alpha with heart, humility, and an understanding of those around him. I'd say his sweet side or his soft side is something that is unique or contrary to the other Skolov Alpha's. He's in tune with his siblings and how they function within the family. He also gives a hand to those who need help and it's his compassion that sets him apart in so many ways. Yes, he's very much an Alpha with all the possessive, protective, and obsessive traits that make him OTT, but he has this sweet charm that, I think sets him apart from his brothers and made him extremely personable. He's compassionate with his younger siblings and he uses their strengths to help lead and teach them. To me, displaying how good of a dad he's going to be, when the time is right. (I do hope the other Skolov's all get a book because I love how much I got to know them in this story).<br /><br />Scarlett is a sweet and sensitive soul, but also strong all rolled into one beautiful and gifted omega. Her protective nature almost makes her a martyr, willing to sacrifice herself to save those she loves. I believe it's her inner strength that shoots out in colors, making her desirable and one of the most wanted omega's in the galaxy. For Damien alone, she really let's her colors splash and he's constantly in awe of her beauty.<br /><br />Damien is also one of the few men Scarlett stands up to, which he both loves and finds annoying. Where most people would cower down at the brute enforcer, it is their familiarity that gives her strength to take on the Alpha. They are both brutal to one another considering the way they parted, both placing blame, though really neither is the cause. However, even with the animosity in the air, in their core there is always a stirring of love and tons of chemistry that shines through even when they say mean things. I love their protective nature and the ultimate caring for each other no matter how much blustering they make. It's the kind of pull that brings me back again and again to Alison's stories.<br /><br />Filthy Royal has twists and turns and is jammed packed with high adrenaline action. Literally, the book is riddled with fights, people to save, buildings crumbling, near death defying escapes, and so much more that I could go on and on. On top of all the action there are is also the burning passion and several deeply emotional moments that Damien and Scarlett share. These two experience a lot together and I loved experiencing it all with them.</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/10209236?shelf=dark-romance" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">dark-romance</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/10209236?shelf=enemies-or-rivals-to-lovers" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">enemies-or-rivals-to-lovers</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/10209236?shelf=fantasy-sci-fi-pnr-supernatural" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">fantasy-sci-fi-pnr-supernatural</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span> <div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium" aria-label="Show all items in the list"><span class="Button__labelItem">...more</span></button></div></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="SocialFooter__statsContai