></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">WOW... Damien and Scarlett's long awaited story is finally out (I gratefully received an advanced reader copy of it)! Normally, I would read Alison's books in a weekend (gorging on them, actually), but this feels like an XXL size book and you will totally get your money's worth! SO, it took me a little longer to read as **this is a story to savor!*** No sneaking bits in between work calls, no. I had to devote some serious ME time to soak it in. ;-)<br /><br />This story takes place in the Golden Dome - a brutal gladiator-type place - or glamorous, depending on your point of view. Like the others in the Ruthless Warlords series, the story has lots of action, some dark themes (slavery of beings is the norm in the Anarchiem universe), fated mates agonizingly separated for years, and there's STEAM. Oh yes, Damien and Scarlett together... mmhmm. The prequel makes this a lovers-to-enemies-to-lovers romance. Obviously, even when they're enemies, the sparks fly. Whoooo - that mud scene! There is some secondary MM romance, but the naughty bits are off-page.<br /><br />Other Skolov family characters feature in this book, so there's still a warm-hearted feeling to this dark romance. They are an awesome, kick-butt family.<br />I won't spoil anything else here, but I am SALIVATING for Anya's story. Ever since his bit part early in the Ruthless Warriors series, I've been fascinated with the idea of a certain uptight Federation officer brought to his knees. Wheeee!</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="stats" class="So