iew","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.99TpeRSJyzpTMm5iyDCYhQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:121973797"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1766950187050,"createdAt":1696971682505,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1698325385694,"text":"“𝚃𝚑𝚎 𝚖𝚘𝚜𝚝 𝚍𝚊𝚗𝚐𝚎𝚛𝚘𝚞𝚜 𝚝𝚑𝚒𝚗𝚐 𝚒𝚗 𝚝𝚑𝚒𝚜 𝚐𝚊𝚕𝚊𝚡𝚢 𝚒𝚜 𝚖𝚎 𝚠𝚑𝚎𝚗 𝙸’𝚖 𝚔𝚎𝚙𝚝 𝚏𝚛𝚘𝚖 𝚢𝚘𝚞.”\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003ci\u003eFilthy Royal \u003c/i\u003emight just be the most intense and twisty book in this series! It was a wild ride from the first page—but one with rich emotion and character growth. (Miraculously, it also managed to sidestep every major complaint I usually have about second chance romances. 🤯)\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e✱::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::✱\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e𝗠𝗠𝗖: Damien, 18➞22, Cage fighter and Enforcer. Fourth brother of the Skolov dynasty, with a lot to prove.\u003cbr /\u003e𝗙𝗠𝗖: Scarlett, 21➞25, Dancer, Omega prize, and secret weapon. Like all the Omega FMCs in this series, she has cool powers. \u003ci\u003e(This will sound random, but she's kinda like a cross between Rainbow-Brite and \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"3966c94f-cbcf-486d-81d8-5060f07a03eb\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"3966c94f-cbcf-486d-81d8-5060f07a03eb\"\u003eQuake (aka Daisy Johnson).\u003c/label\u003e)\u003c/i\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e𝗡𝗼𝘁𝗲𝘀:\u003ci\u003e\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003eomegaverse\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003einsta/fated mates\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003ebetrayal\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003esecond chance\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003ejealous/ possessive/ protective/ tortured mmc\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003eprotective/ tortured fmc\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003einterrogation\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003esecrets+plot twists\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003erut haze\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003edirty talk+praise\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003eenemies while lovers\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003edanger banging\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003edouble virgins\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003ehigh action\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003ci\u003e\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003efree on Kobo Plus\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003e~149k words\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003e568 Kindle pages\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003e17:05 audiobook\u003cb\u003e | \u003c/b\u003e\u003c/i\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e✱::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::✱\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThe first third of \u003ci\u003eFilthy Royal \u003c/i\u003e is actually a prequel. That may sound like overkill, but it really works here, for two main reasons: For one, we get to see all of their early relationship 'firsts'. With most second chances, I usually feel partially cheated out of those milestones.\u003ci\u003e (C'mon—what's better than New Relationship Energy?)\u003c/i\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eFor another, fewer flashbacks! In fairness, flashbacks can be powerful. For example, each flashback in \u003ci\u003eRuthless King\u003c/i\u003e was a clue that advanced the plot. But second chance books are notorious for shoehorning in momentum-killing flashbacks. But here, we live each stolen moment in their (temporarily) doomed whirlwind love affair. 🥹\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e... NGL it's heartbreaking that they were apart four hellish years. That said, the logic behind their separation was actually solid. There really weren't any good alternatives, something that becomes even more evident once the whole story comes out. Also, it kills me to say this because I loved younger Damien, \u003ci\u003ebut... \u003c/i\u003eHe truly was too immature, too hot-headed, to navigate the situation they were in at the time. Even if Scarlett had made different choices, it likely would've ended worse for them. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eWhen they meet up again, rut haze comes on hard—at the same time all hells break loose. They're in the middle of a battle, horny and totally unhinged—and Damien's poor brother Maddox has to keep them alive while trying to talk them down 💀. It was intense but also kinda hilarious. Maddox had some great comic moments in this book. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eUnderstandably, Damien is still tortured and furious over the events in the prequel, but it was tough to witness how cruel he sometimes seemed. (Thankfully, it was more bark than bite.) And I was a little frustrated by Scarlett's fatalism and distrust, but she also had good reasons. They had so many obstacles, both internal and external—but it made for a very hard-won HEA.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e✱::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::✱\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e🎙\u003c/b\u003e𝗔𝘂𝗱𝗶𝗼 𝗡𝗼𝘁𝗲𝘀: I got the chance to listen to an advanced copy, and it's epic. Just like the previous three books, it's narrated in \u003cb\u003eduet \u003c/b\u003eby Jason Clarke and Stella Hunter. IYKYK—but in case you're not familiar, they are two of the best narrators around. Duet narration always brings an extra layer of realism, and combined with such powerful acting—holy hell, I was totally hooked. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis book in particular really plays to Jason's range. He's pitch-perfect for the flirty, playful energy of younger Damien—and the tortured, jaded Alpha he matures into. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAnd really, there's nothing Jason Clarke's voice can't do. He could narrate a livestream of paint drying, and I'd be captivated. He could read the U.S. Tax Code, and I'd be riveted. He could narrate a cookbook on \u003ci\u003eboiling water\u003c/i\u003e, and I'd feel the steam... \u003ci\u003eOkay, okay... \u003c/i\u003eI'll quit before it gets weird. 😝\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e✱::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::✱\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e🚦 Safety (⚠ 𝒔𝒑𝒐𝒊𝒍𝒆𝒓𝒔!):\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e» 𝙢𝙖𝙞𝙣 𝙥𝙪𝙧𝙨𝙪𝙚𝙧: MMC\u003cbr /\u003e» 𝙤𝙬 / 𝙤𝙢 / 𝙤𝙥: Some OM. At the end of the prequel, Scarlett \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"fddfff94-0c9b-4309-965b-b7aaee85ece3\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"fddfff94-0c9b-4309-965b-b7aaee85ece3\"\u003eis forced to marry—but it's a lavender marriage. so she and Kadon are just friends. Contractually speaking, there's cheating on both sides, but neither of them consider it to be. It takes a while before Damien learns the whole story, so he's wildly jealous.\u003c/label\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e» 𝙥𝙪𝙨𝙝 / 𝙥𝙪𝙡𝙡 / 𝙖𝙣𝙜𝙨𝙩: So much angst, I had to remind myself a few times that there would be an HEA! In general: For the first third (prequel), \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"aae5bfde-fdc2-4970-b07f-d5b4dd6221ab\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"aae5bfde-fdc2-4970-b07f-d5b4dd6221ab\"\u003eDamien pursues hard and Scarlett is wary. In the middle third, both push away for different reasons. In the last third, Damien is all-in.\u003c/label\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e» 𝙨𝙚𝙥𝙖𝙧𝙖𝙩𝙞𝙤𝙣: Yes, a four-year separation following the prequel. After that, \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"497176ae-1051-4475-a786-c3a16a33f2ce\" /\u003e\u003clabe